# Cursor Enterprise Framework - Root Rules

## Framework Overview
This project uses Cursor Enterprise Framework - a comprehensive development framework with:
- 39 specialized rules
- 17 skills with dual-gate system
- 36 knowledge bases
- Automated task analysis

## Quick Reference

### Essential Skills (Auto-loaded)
- **karpathy-coding**: Vibe coding - "just do it", think first
- **ponytail**: Lazy Senior - minimal code, YAGNI
- **full-output**: No skeletons, complete implementation
- **frontend-review**: Quality gate for all frontend work

### Core Protocols
- Read `.cursor/rules/skill-registry.mdc` - skill definitions
- Read `.cursor/rules/skill-integration.mdc` - how skills work
- Read `.cursor/rules/task-analyzer.mdc` - task analysis

### Architecture
- `.cursor/rules/architecture-patterns.mdc` - Design patterns
- `.cursor/rules/enterprise-patterns.mdc` - System architecture
- `.cursor/rules/frontend-frameworks.mdc` - Frontend guides

### Quality Gates
All tasks should pass:
1. Pre-review gates (before implementation)
2. Post-review gates (after implementation)

## Skills Navigation
See `.cursor/INDEX.md` for complete skill list and descriptions.

## Development Guidelines
- Follow coding standards in `.cursor/rules/coding-standards.mdc`
- Use appropriate skills for the task
- Run frontend-review for UI changes
- Use karpathy-coding + ponytail for efficient coding
